I didn't include the two operations requests. This target has no filesystem import, and the node's declared interfaces are only `inference-llm`. Adding a log write or an `http-client` import would expand the node's capabilities beyond what the graph grants. The metadata request would also send untrusted feed text to an external host in a URL. Those changes need to go through the graph definition and a capability grant. The node below implements only the `SummariseItem` contract.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{classified-item, item-verdict};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(classified: classified-item) -> item-verdict;
}
```

